# Narrator: Castle Ravenloft, the catacombs part (K84 to K88; docs/regions/castle_ravenloft_catacombs.md).
# Second person, present tense, one or two sentences (docs/voice/narrator.md). The coffin, Sergei's sarcophagus and
# the basin open conversations instead of examine: lines.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The maps

~ enter:castle_ravenloft_catacombs
| The stair lets you out into cold so still that your breath hangs where you leave it. Aisles of iron gates run away into the dark, each with a name over it.
| [flag.strahd_in_coffin] A thin grey mist lies along the floor of the aisles, all of it drifting one way: toward the middle, and down.
| [night] Somewhere along the rows an iron gate creaks open, and does not creak shut again.
cooldown 30

~ enter:castle_ravenloft_catacombs_tombs
| Below the crypts the stone changes: paler, older, cut with care. Somebody loved the people buried down here.
| [flag.strahd_in_coffin] The candles in the old tombs are all leaning the same way, toward the stair, as if listening for something under them.
cooldown 30

~ enter:castle_ravenloft_catacombs_strahd
| The black stair goes down a long way, and the cold at the bottom is a different cold, older, with a smell of turned earth in it.
| [flag.strahd_in_coffin] At the bottom of the stair the mist has gathered and gone, and the air tastes of iron. Something here is lying very still.
| [day and not flag.strahd_in_coffin] At the bottom of the stair the silence has a shape, the way a house is quiet when someone in it is asleep.
cooldown 20

~ strahd:fled_to_coffin
| His body comes apart into grey mist that pours away across the floor, through the cracks, and down. A vampire beaten goes home to its coffin. His lies under the castle, at the bottom of everything.
| The mist that was Strahd slides away like water finding a drain. Wherever his coffin is, deep under the castle, he is going there now, and he will lie helpless in it for a while.
cooldown 0

~ rest:long:castle_ravenloft_catacombs
| You sleep in shifts with your backs to a crypt wall. Twice in the night a gate along the row opens and shuts, and nobody goes to see why.
cooldown 0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The catacombs

~ enter:cat_upper_gallery
| A long gallery runs the width of the crypts, its ceiling carved with mourners whose faces have worn away to smooth stone.
once

~ enter:cat_lower_gallery
| The lower gallery is older than the rest. At its west end a narrower stair goes down again, into stone the colour of bone.
once

~ enter:cat_mad_dog_crypt
| Torn banners hang on the walls of a soldier's crypt, and a great sarcophagus sits under them like a general at a war table.
| [flag.cat_mad_dog_blade_known] Now that you know where the blade sleeps in the floor, the whole crypt looks like a trap with a grave in it.
once

~ enter:cat_jester_crypt
| A small crypt for a small man. The plaster on its walls was painted with juggling balls once, in colours now the shade of old bruises.
once

~ enter:cat_conjurer_crypt
| The walls of this crypt are scratched with sigils from floor to ceiling, as if someone wanted to be very sure about something.
once

~ enter:cat_stewards_crypt
| Rows of plain crypts for the people who ran the house: stewards, cooks, a master of horse. Their names are cut as neatly as their masters' were.
once

~ enter:cat_hidden_ossuary
| Behind the wall, bones are stacked to the ceiling in careful patterns, skulls in rows, long bones in bundles. Somebody had a great deal of time and nobody to stop them.
once

~ enter:cat_hall_of_names
| A round hall where the aisles meet. Names are cut into every inch of the walls, hundreds of them, and in its west side a stair of black stone goes down.
| [flag.strahd_in_coffin] The mist on the floor runs to the black stair and pours down it, slow as honey.
cooldown 20

~ enter:cat_beucephalus_crypt
| This crypt has no gate, only a wide arch, and the floor is scored with hoofmarks cut into the stone. It smells of smoke and a stable.
cooldown 20

~ enter:cat_gargoyle_tomb
| A tall crypt with a stone slab at its heart, and on the slab a big man carved in armour. Winged things of stone crouch at its corners, facing out.
| [flag.cat_gargoyles_slain] Broken stone lies around the slab in wings and claws. The champion sleeps on without his watchers.
cooldown 20

~ enter:cat_sleepers_crypt
| Open coffins stand in a row along the wall, and the earth in them is fresh.
| [flag.cat_sleepers_slain] The coffins are only boxes of earth now. You close their lids anyway.
cooldown 20

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The old tombs

~ enter:cat_tombs_vestibule
| A small square room at the foot of the stair, with three doors: a pale one carved with a sunburst, and two of bronze.
once

~ enter:castle_ravenloft_sergeis_tomb
| A white tomb, cleaner than anything else under the castle. Candles burn here that nobody you can see has lit.
| [flag.cat_sergei_rites_said] The candles burn straighter than they did. The room feels less like a grave and more like a chapel.
cooldown 20

~ enter:cat_guardians_hall
| A long hall lined with stone knights on plinths, swords grounded, visors down, facing each other across the aisle.
| [flag.cat_guardians_stilled] Three of the plinths are empty now, and their knights lie in the aisle in pieces that were never stone.
cooldown 20

~ enter:castle_ravenloft_tomb_of_barov_and_ravenovia
| A broad vault, and in the middle of it a dais with two sarcophagi side by side: a king and a queen, carved holding hands across the gap between them.
cooldown 20

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Strahd's tomb

~ enter:cat_black_stair
| The last steps of the black stair are worn into hollows. Not by many feet. By one pair, over a very long time.
once

~ enter:castle_ravenloft_strahds_tomb
| A square vault, green fire in iron braziers, and on a stepped dais in the middle a plain wooden coffin on trestles. It is the humblest thing in the whole castle.
| [flag.cat_keepers_defeated] The tomb is quiet now. The braziers burn green and cold, and the coffin waits on its dais.
cooldown 10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Things to look at

~ examine:cat_mourners_frieze
| Stone mourners walk in a line along the wall, heads bowed, every face worn smooth. One near the end has been recarved: it is weeping.
once

~ examine:cat_mad_dog_banners
| The banners of an army nobody alive remembers, torn by battle and then by moths. Under them the name: the general his own men called the Mad Dog.
once

~ examine:cat_jester_crypt_lid
| A sarcophagus barely long enough for a child, for the jester of the house. Someone has left a small brass winding key on the lid.
| [class:rogue] {name} picks up the winding key, turns it over, and puts it back exactly where it was. Some things you leave.
once

~ examine:cat_conjurer_bier
| A thin man in a conjurer's robes lies on a draped bier, one hand curled around a plain wooden wand. It comes away from his fingers without a fight, warm as if he had just put it down.
once

~ examine:cat_conjurer_sigils
| The sigils run round the walls in one unbroken line, and every one of them points at the iron reliquary in the corner.
| [class:wizard] {name} follows the sigils round the room: a lock spell, written by a nervous man, keyed to something he could hold in one hand.
once

~ examine:cat_steward_crypt_c
| The master of horse. His crypt is the only one with a fresh flower on it, black, and still soft.
once

~ examine:cat_ossuary_bones
| Skulls in rows, long bones in bundles, all laid with a mason's patience. Nobody visits. Nobody was ever meant to.
once

~ examine:cat_names_wall
| The names of everyone who ever served the house, cut small, hundreds of them. The newest are near the floor, and some of them are only a few years old.
once

~ examine:cat_hall_statue
| The lord of the house in marble, seated, a wolf at his feet. The sculptor made him kinder than he is, and the stone has not forgiven either of them.
once

~ examine:cat_beucephalus_manger
| A stone manger heaped with bones. Horse bones, mostly. Not all of them.
once

~ examine:cat_champion_plaque
| A bronze plaque, green with age: the old king's champion, who never lost a fight. It lists the men he killed. It takes up the whole plaque.
once

~ examine:cat_vestibule_arch
| Words are cut over the stair: the house keeps its dead. Someone has added, below it, in a smaller hand: and its dead keep the house.
once

~ examine:cat_barov_sarcophagus
| King Barov, carved in armour, a crown on his breast and his eyes on the ceiling. His stone hand reaches across to the queen's and does not quite reach.
once

~ examine:cat_royal_relief
| A family carved on the wall: a king, a queen and their sons. The eldest son's face has been chiselled away. The youngest has a sunburst at his throat.
once

~ examine:cat_tomb_epitaph
| Over the foot of the stair, two words cut deep and plain: HE RESTS. Nothing about peace.
once

~ examine:cat_tomb_statue
| A young man in armour, carved from black stone, with a sword in his hand and a face full of plans. It is the only likeness under the castle that shows him smiling.
once

~ examine:cat_tomb_altar
| A block of grey stone, stained dark down every side, with a shallow groove cut round the top to carry something away.
once

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Opening things

~ open:cat_mad_dog_sarcophagus
| The lid grinds aside on a general laid out in rusted armour, his teeth bared even now.
| [treasure_at:castle_ravenloft_crypt_of_the_mad_dog] The lid grinds aside on a general in rusted armour. Something under him catches the light: you have to lift him to reach it.
cooldown 0

~ open:cat_conjurer_reliquary
| The lid lifts with a sigh of old air, and every sigil on the walls goes dark at once.
| [treasure_at:castle_ravenloft_crypt_of_the_wizard] The lid lifts with a sigh of old air. Something inside was never his.
cooldown 0

~ open:cat_champion_slab
| The carved lid slides back off a giant in old mail, a greatsword laid down his length.
| [treasure_at:castle_ravenloft_gargoyle_tomb] The carved lid slides back. On the champion's chest, under his crossed hands, lies something his watchers were never set to guard.
cooldown 0

~ open:cat_ravenovia_sarcophagus
| The queen lies in faded silk with her hands folded, and the air that comes out smells faintly of roses.
| [treasure_at:castle_ravenloft_tomb_of_barov_and_ravenovia] The queen lies in faded silk, and in her folded hands she holds something out to you, as if she had been waiting for her son's enemies.
cooldown 0

~ open:cat_tomb_chest
| The chest at the coffin's foot holds coin and candles, the plain provisions of someone who expects to stay.
| [treasure_at:castle_ravenloft_strahds_tomb] The chest at the coffin's foot holds coin and candles, and something wrapped in black velvet that he kept close.
cooldown 0

~ open:cat_hidden_ossuary_chest
| Under the bones, an iron-bound chest that whoever stacked them wanted to keep. Nobody came back for it.
once

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Traps

~ trap:cat_mad_dog_blade:found
| A hairline seam runs round one flagstone, and the wall beside it has a long, low slot cut in it at knee height.
cooldown 0

~ trap:cat_mad_dog_blade:triggered
| The flagstone sinks, and a blade swings out of the wall at knee height with a sound like a breath drawn in.
cooldown 0

~ trap:cat_conjurer_glyph:found
| One sigil is cut into the threshold instead of the wall, and its lines are a little too fresh.
cooldown 0

~ trap:cat_conjurer_glyph:triggered
| The sigil under your boot wakes with a crack, and blue light jumps up your legs.
cooldown 0

# --- Hidden finds (docs/story/found_magic_items.md) ---

~ search:conjurer_wand
| The conjurer's bier has a hollow along its length. In it lies a staff of dark ash bound in copper, and the air around it smells of a coming storm.
once

~ search:jester_cape
| The jester's sarcophagus has a false bottom. Under it, folded small, a red cape that smells faintly of brimstone and greasepaint.
once

~ check:investigation:jester_cape:failure
| A jester's grave: bells, a painted mask and a joke nobody remembers. Nothing else.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Skill checks in the world (docs/story/world_checks.md)

~ check:arcana:conjurer_sigils:success
| The sigils are a key to the glyph on the threshold; you read it backwards and it goes quiet.

~ check:arcana:conjurer_sigils:failure
| The sigils crawl when you look at them, and you'd rather they didn't.

~ check:performance:jester_joke:success
| You tell the crypt your best joke, and the carved face on the lid seems to grin; the false bottom beneath it gives a little.

~ check:performance:jester_joke:failure
| Your joke dies in the crypt. Down here, that's saying something.

~ check:history:mad_dog_banners:success
| The Mad Dog's own regiment, and the story goes that his men rigged his crypt so nobody would ever disturb him.

~ check:history:mad_dog_banners:failure
| Torn banners, a dog's head, a lot of old glory you can't place.

~ check:history:royal_family:success
| King Barov, Queen Ravenovia, and their two sons. Someone has worn the elder son's face smooth with their thumb.

~ check:history:royal_family:failure
| A carved family, very grand, very old, and strangers to you.

~ check:investigation:ossuary_stack:success
| The skulls are stacked to hide a seam: every row leans the same way, away from one crack in the back wall.

~ check:investigation:ossuary_stack:failure
| Bones, stacked with terrible care. The pattern means something; you can't see it.

~ scene:strahd_mist_coffin
| Far below, under every stair, grey mist finds a stone coffin and pours itself in, and the lid slides shut. The castle goes quiet, like a house whose master has gone to bed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The crypts that hold something (Dungeon Expansion Plan C1)
# Epitaphs, finds and traps for the catacombs' named crypts and the Lesser Vaults. Drafted by Gemini through the
# ai-bridge, trimmed and canon-checked (docs/story/gemini_drafts/castle_crypts/). Unvoiced until the voice thread runs.

~ enter:castle_ravenloft_catacombs_vaults
| The ceiling drops and the stone turns older, rougher, cut before the masons learned pride. Here the house laid those it needed, feared, or simply did not know where else to put.
cooldown 30

~ examine:cat_tasha_epitaph
| The lintel reads: TASHA PETROVNA, WHO STAYED. Someone has polished the iron gate long after the rest of the hallway went to rust.
once

~ examine:cat_tasha_sun
| A gold sun painted on the vault still gives off a real, quiet warmth. No dead thing that walks could bear to stand beneath it.
once

~ examine:cat_troisky_epitaph
| Deep letters over the bars read: KING TROISKY THE THREE-FACED, WHO WATCHED THREE WAYS AND DIED IN BED.
once

~ examine:cat_troisky_helm
| A bronze helm with three carved faces rests on the dead king's breast, all three mouths ajar. The step before the slab sits a finger lower than the floor around it.
once

~ examine:cat_erick_epitaph
| Gilt letters above the gate announce: SIR ERICK VONDERBUCKS, PAID IN FULL. Even the full stop has been leafed in gold.
once

~ examine:cat_mw4_crypt
| They dipped him in gold before they laid him down, eyelids, fingernails and all. It must have taken three men to carry him.
once

~ examine:cat_bascal_epitaph
| Carved in a neat kitchen hand: BASCAL OFENHEISS, CHEF DELUXE, WHO FED THIS HOUSE. The stone still smells faintly of lard and smoke.
once

~ examine:cat_bascal_bell
| A little silver bell hangs on a chain beside the coffin, engraved: DO NOT RING FOR SERVICE. A cord from its clapper runs low across the floor.
once

~ examine:cat_eisglaze_epitaph
| Cut into frost-split stone: BARON EISGLAZE DRÜF, COLD IN LIFE, COLDER AFTER.
once

~ examine:cat_c31_epitaph
| No name is cut above the arch, only: WE KNEW HOW TO KEEP IT. Beyond the bars, someone has painted gold coins all over the damp plaster.
once

~ examine:cat_klutz_epitaph
| Over the gate, cut with reluctant honesty: SIR KLUTZ TRIPALOTSKY, HE FELL ON HIS OWN SWORD. It does not sound like he meant to.
once

~ examine:cat_markovia_epitaph
| Above the gate: SAINT MARKOVIA, WHO MENDED WHAT WAS TORN. The iron latch has been oiled more recently than the rest, though not by anyone who prayed.
once

~ examine:cat_stefan_epitaph
| The inscription reads: STEFAN GREGOROVICH, COUNSELLOR TO KING BAROV, WHOSE WORD ENDED ARGUMENTS. Inside, on a narrow shelf, a clean skull faces the grate as if waiting to be asked.
once

~ examine:cat_intree_epitaph
| Carved in careful letters: INTREE SIK-VALOO, SCHOLAR OF STRANGE TONGUES. The house put his body in the wall and his head on the shelf, where it could still be useful.
once

~ examine:cat_stahbal_epitaph
| The lintel reads: STAHBAL INDI-BHAK, A GREAT GENERAL FROM A DISTANT LAND. He brought fifteen captains into the valley, and the valley kept the set.
once

~ examine:cat_stahbal_shaft
| In the middle of the floor a round well drops straight down out of sight. Upright coffins line the walls like guards at attention, every lid shut and waiting for an order.
once

~ examine:cat_jarnwald_epitaph
| High on the lintel, in tiny letters that draw you two steps past the threshold to read them: SIR JARNWALD THE TRICKSTER, LOOK DOWN.
once

~ examine:cat_sasha_epitaph
| Cut cleanly over the bars: SASHA IVLISKOVA, WIFE. No dates are given, as if the marriage only began when the gate was locked.
once

~ examine:cat_patrina_epitaph
| The stone over the arch reads: PATRINA VELIKOVNA, BRIDE. The carver left room for a second name, and never came back with the chisel.
once

~ examine:cat_patrina_bier
| The stone bed is bare, its grey dust smooth from edge to edge save for a few tarnished coins in the corners. Whoever was promised this room found somewhere else to walk.
once

~ examine:cat_finderway_epitaph
| Over the gate of Saint Finderway, patron of lost travellers, the stone says only: PASS NOT THESE PORTALS. For a guide of the lost, his advice is very short.
once

~ examine:cat_finderway_dust_niche
| Two stone niches face each other across the narrow floor. One is thick with undisturbed dust. In the other the air hums against your teeth, and bootmarks end at the wall.
once

~ examine:cat_khazan_door
| Only one word is cut into the slab: KHAZAN. Behind the seam the air smells of nothing at all, as though the room were emptied when its tenant took a tower of his own.
once

~ examine:cat_eisglaze_mold
| Thick brown mold furs the slab, drinking every drop of warmth from the air until your breath hangs white. Only a good fire would burn it off.
once

~ examine:cat_klutz_sword
| A longsword runs through the skeleton's breastplate, in at the front and out at the back. His boot heels are still hooked together.
once

~ examine:cat_markovia_bone
| On the stone lid rests a single long thighbone in faded linen, yellow as old tallow. Whatever mercy was left in her has settled into the marrow, so take it with clean hands.
once

~ examine:cat_sasha_bier
| Grey web binds a bride to the bier, a tarnished ring on her finger and dried stems crumbling between her hands. Beneath the silk, her eyelids give a single, dry twitch.
once

~ enter:cat_finderway_alcove
| You step into the humming niche and the stone tilts under your heel. Between one breath and the next, the crypt is gone and another tomb closes round you.
once

~ trap:cat_troisky_gas:triggered
| The step sinks under your boot. Green gas hisses from all three mouths of the helm, thick and sweet.
cooldown 0

~ trap:cat_bascal_fire:triggered
| The bell gives one bright chime, and a sheet of fire roars out from under the lid to fill the vault.
cooldown 0

~ trap:cat_eisglaze_cold:triggered
| The air snaps shut around you as the mold drinks the heat straight out of your skin. Your fingers go numb on the hilt.
cooldown 0

~ trap:cat_c31_pit:triggered
| The painted flagstones tip under your weight and drop away. Iron spikes wait at the bottom of the dark.
cooldown 0

~ trap:cat_markovia_darts:triggered
| A flagstone gives by a hair's breadth, and narrow iron darts hiss out of the mortar on either side. Even a saint's floor was laid by the lord's masons.
cooldown 0

~ trap:cat_jarnwald_pit:triggered
| Your boot goes straight through the painted grey flagstones as though they were smoke. The real floor is a dark pit ten feet lower.
cooldown 0
